{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-020-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteRunCostCalculatorTests.cs","line":198,"method":"SupersededRecovery_ExcludedByElsInput","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteRunCostCalculator.cs:143; stubbing supersede/ELS filtering leaves this green because the els list is pre-filtered by the test -> green; only removing the tree-membership check -> red","what_it_asserts":"Sums a one-row els list the test itself built without the superseded row; asserts sum=2000, count=1.","why_weak":"The named behavior (superseded recovery excluded) lives in EffectiveState.ComputeELS, which this test never calls, so no realistic supersede regression reds it.","proposed_action":"Delete as covered by RecoveryFromDifferentTree_Excluded, or rewrite to drive EffectiveState.ComputeELS with an installed supersede relation and feed the real ELS output.","effort":"M","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-020-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteRunCostCalculatorTests.cs","line":125,"method":"RecoveryInTreeButNotRouteMembers_StillCounted","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteRunCostCalculator.cs:143; dropping the treeMembers Contains check leaves THIS cell green (its row is in treeMembers) while RecoveryFromDifferentTree_Excluded reds -> green (Phase 2 corrected string; the cell pins less than its name claims)","what_it_asserts":"A recovery row whose id is a tree member but not a route member is summed (5400, count 1), plus a self-assertion that the id is absent from route.RecordingIds.","why_weak":"SumRecoveredCredits takes the scope set as a parameter and reads route only for logging (line 110), so the G1 rescoping regression the comment names cannot be introduced here; the real guard is ResolveTreeRecordingIds.","proposed_action":"Retitle and recomment to state it pins parameter-scoped membership, or move the G1 claim onto a Compute() level test that builds the scope through ResolveTreeRecordingIds.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none","note":"Phase 2: original falsifiability string was wrong; corrected."}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"RouteRunCostCalculator","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteRunCostCalculator.cs","sut_line":257,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"Compute_SupersededRecoveryRow_ExcludedByRealEls","sketch":"Install a ParsekScenario carrying a RecordingSupersedeRelation over the recovering recording, add both recordings via RecordingStore.AddRecordingWithTreeForTesting, ledger a Recovery FundsEarning row on the superseded id, then call Compute with EffectiveState.ComputeELS() and assert RecoveredCredits stays 0.","guards":"A supersede-filtering regression in ELS silently re-crediting a retired recovery into a route run cost.","risk":"career"}
